# Git: branches before multi-file work

Full policy: [docs/GIT_WORKFLOW.md](../../docs/GIT_WORKFLOW.md)

## Rules

1. **Never commit directly to `main`** — always branch first
2. **One Linear issue = one branch** — name: `feat/LOG-XX-description`
3. **One concern per branch** — don't mix unrelated areas
4. **Push the branch** after commits — `git push -u origin <branch>`
5. **Merge via GitHub PR** — squash merge preferred
6. **No force-push to `main`** without explicit human instruction
7. **Never commit** `.env`, secrets, or machine-local IDE state

## Branch naming

| Prefix | Use for | Example |
|--------|---------|---------|
| `feat/` | New feature | `feat/LOG-42-auth-flow` |
| `fix/` | Bug fix | `fix/LOG-51-secret-rotation` |
| `chore/` | Tooling/deps | `chore/update-deps` |
| `docs/` | Docs only | `docs/api-guide` |

## Quick start

```bash
git fetch origin && git checkout main && git pull origin main
git checkout -b feat/LOG-XX-short-description
# ... work ...
git push -u origin feat/LOG-XX-short-description
# Open PR → main on GitHub
```
